  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The rear extension on this proposal, by reason of scale and siting, would result in detrimental harm to the neighbouring property. Specifically, it has resulted in a material loss of sunlight/daylight, and unacceptable overshadowing and overbearing impacts on 113 &amp; 117 Wood Lane, therefore constituting unneighbourly development and contrary to: </p><p>- National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023); </p><p>- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021); </p><p>- Policy CP3 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010);</p><p>- Policy BP8 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011); </p><p>- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD6 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021); </p><p>- The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (February 2012).<br></p>"
  ],
